WEBVTT


00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:07.157
<i>SiNCRONiZACiON POR
~ N3krA ~
SEPTiCEMiA TEAM
.::Piratas Con Los Patines::.</i>


00:01:07.158 --> 00:01:13.205
<i>Some chefs call them "lovebirds,"
a romantic dish for that special occasion.</i>


00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:21.213
<i>Properly cooked,
they're as tender as butter.</i>


00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.426
<i>They can be roasted,
stuffed with wild rice or barley...</i>


00:01:25.593 --> 00:01:27.470
<i>...or you can broil them, poach them...</i>


00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.765
<i>...barbecue them,
and even braise them.</i>


00:01:30.973 --> 00:01:34.226
<i>But there's no greater sin
than to overcook a quail.</i>


00:01:34.852 --> 00:01:39.607
<i>Perfectly cooked, it must have
a touch of pink on the breast.</i>


00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:44.070
<i>But you need the right quail. It has
to be fleshy or it dries out too easily.</i>


00:01:44.278 --> 00:01:46.113
<i>I prefer to serve them roasted.</i>


00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:49.700
That makes their taste richer
and more robust.


00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:52.411
And a side of truffle ravioli
and wild mushrooms...


00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.872
...goes deliciously well with them.


00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:57.917
Of course, you can also cook
them in a pig's bladder...


00:01:58.125 --> 00:02:00.878
...in a mix of Madeira and cognac.


00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:05.466
You see, the bladder helps protect
the quail, keeps it moist.


00:02:05.674 --> 00:02:10.137
You could serve it with a tender sauce
of thyme, spring onions...


00:02:10.388 --> 00:02:12.598
...caramelized shallots, truffles.


00:02:12.807 --> 00:02:15.601
Truffles go perfectly
with almost any quail dish...


00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.771
...because they elevate
the delicate taste.


00:02:19.688 --> 00:02:21.273
Are you feeling okay?


00:02:21.482 --> 00:02:24.527
I'm fine. Go on.


00:02:25.694 --> 00:02:29.198
They wonderfully elevate
the delicate taste of the quail.


00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:32.535
But you have to really
be able to afford truffles...


00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.413
...otherwise you just
better forget about it.


00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:38.499
- Now, for a appetizer, I suggest...
- Kate, would you mind...


00:02:38.708 --> 00:02:42.294
...if I change the subject for a moment?
- No.


00:02:42.503 --> 00:02:44.463
Why do you come to see me
every week?


00:02:45.214 --> 00:02:47.800
My boss said she'd fire me
if I didn't get therapy.


00:02:48.008 --> 00:02:51.470
And why do you think
she thinks you need therapy?


00:02:51.721 --> 00:02:53.305
Why?


00:02:53.848 --> 00:02:55.307
You know what?


00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:58.436
I haven't the faintest idea.


00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:16.704
Ordering two tasting menus.
Fire two amuse-bouche.


00:03:16.912 --> 00:03:20.332
Leah, I need a quail and a Dover sole
for table nine.


00:03:20.541 --> 00:03:24.211
I'm still waiting on those beef
tenderloins. Where are they? Pick up!


00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.422
Terrine, carpaccio.


00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:32.219
Excuse me, you should know
Hal Reeves says the lamb...


00:03:32.428 --> 00:03:35.598
...has never been so good before.
- Really? And what would he know?


00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:39.435
Kate, the Petersons are here. They
wanna tell you how brilliant you are.


00:03:39.643 --> 00:03:42.521
- Brilliant chefs belong in the kitchen.
- At least say hello.


00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:45.066
You know they're some
of my best customers.


00:03:45.274 --> 00:03:48.277
In a minute. Just don't cook them
too long, because they get...


00:03:48.486 --> 00:03:50.696
- They get tough, I know.
- No, dry. Dry, Leah.


00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.531
I get tough. Quail get dry.


00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:55.534
Kate, I wanna go
over the menu for next week.


00:03:56.452 --> 00:03:57.995
Later, okay?


00:04:06.587 --> 00:04:08.255
<i>You're a magician, Kate.</i>


00:04:08.464 --> 00:04:11.092
And you know my husband sings
your praises constantly.


00:04:11.258 --> 00:04:13.094
In fact, it's hard not to be jealous.


00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.138
I worship anyone
who can surprise my palate.


00:04:16.347 --> 00:04:18.557
It's always a pleasure
to cook for you both.


00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:21.060
- We'll see you next week, right?
- Of course.


00:04:21.268 --> 00:04:23.270
- Good night.
- Good night.


00:04:30.611 --> 00:04:32.363
Nice to see you.


00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:34.573
I'm telling you
it's not cooked properly.


00:04:34.782 --> 00:04:37.368
- May I ask what this is about?
- Kate, I'll handle this.


00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:39.078
- I take it you're the chef?
- Yes.


00:04:39.286 --> 00:04:42.039
- There's something I'd like to show you.
- Don't do this.


00:04:42.206 --> 00:04:44.667
My wife's foie gras
hasn't been cooked long enough.


00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:46.627
- Excuse me?
- Why don't I bring you...


00:04:46.794 --> 00:04:50.089
...a new appetizer with my compliments?
- It's cooked just fine.


00:04:50.297 --> 00:04:53.634
Nothing to be ashamed of, honey.
Even the best stumble over foie gras.


00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:56.971
<i>There's nothing wrong with this.
It's precisely comme il faut.</i>


00:04:57.179 --> 00:05:00.349
<i>- What is that supposed to mean?
- Comme il faut? "As it should be. "</i>


00:05:00.516 --> 00:05:04.019
140 degrees in the oven, 80 degrees
water temperature, for 25 minutes...


00:05:04.186 --> 00:05:07.648
...not too long, not too short,
with the perfect touch of pink, honey.


00:05:07.857 --> 00:05:11.193
That's it.
We'll take our business somewhere else.


00:05:11.402 --> 00:05:12.987
Let's go.


00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:19.118
May I suggest Vinnie's hot dog stand
at the corner? He cooks to order.


00:05:21.203 --> 00:05:22.747
<i>How many times have I told you?</i>


00:05:22.913 --> 00:05:26.042
You can't make a scene every time
someone doesn't like your food.


00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.878
- Please. The guy's a barbarian.
- And a paying customer.


00:05:29.045 --> 00:05:31.255
If he says the foie gras
is not done, it's not.


00:05:31.505 --> 00:05:34.008
- Foie gras is cruelty to animals.
- Stay out of this.


00:05:34.175 --> 00:05:38.345
I swear to God, if you weren't one of the
better chefs in this city, I'd fire you.


00:05:38.512 --> 00:05:41.682
One of the better chefs?
What's that supposed to mean?


00:05:41.891 --> 00:05:43.893
I bet she's just saying that
to annoy me.


00:05:45.519 --> 00:05:48.230
She's just saying that to annoy me.


00:05:48.439 --> 00:05:50.566
- Isn't she?
- Whatever you say, chef.


00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:29.105
<i>Mailbox one. You have no messages.</i>


00:06:45.287 --> 00:06:46.956
- Hey, how are you?
- I'm good, Frank.


00:06:47.123 --> 00:06:48.874
Got some nice lobsters from Maine.


00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:51.335
That one's a little too small.
Try this one.


00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:54.797
Yeah, yeah. Have them delivered
by 2:30, okay?


00:06:55.005 --> 00:06:57.133
And send those scrawny ones
to La Fontaine.


00:06:57.341 --> 00:07:00.052
Kate! Who's your best friend?


00:07:00.302 --> 00:07:02.680
- You got it?
- Did you ask me to?


00:07:02.888 --> 00:07:04.640
Golden tilefish?


00:07:05.516 --> 00:07:07.268
- Bob!
- Just for you.


00:07:07.476 --> 00:07:11.355
- It's beautiful.
- Beautiful golden tilefish, line-caught.


00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:12.898
- Beautiful.
- Give me a kiss.


00:07:13.149 --> 00:07:15.025
- Bob.
- Give me a kiss.


00:07:15.651 --> 00:07:19.280
- Hey! Hey! How come I didn't get a kiss?
- How come you didn't get a kiss?


00:07:19.488 --> 00:07:20.823
You ain't got the goods.


00:07:21.032 --> 00:07:23.325
- What's this?
- I don't see any golden tilefish.


00:07:34.545 --> 00:07:36.547
<i>- Hello?
- Hey, it's me.</i>


00:07:36.714 --> 00:07:39.759
I'm just checking in.
We should be there about 9.


00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:41.927
<i>Great, so I'll make sure
I'm back by then.</i>


00:07:42.178 --> 00:07:45.681
Okay, cool. So, what are you doing?
Reading a recipe, right?


00:07:46.724 --> 00:07:49.935
Christine, don't be ridiculous.
I do have other interests.


00:07:50.186 --> 00:07:52.063
<i>Of course you do. Name one.</i>


00:07:52.229 --> 00:07:54.523
<i>- How's Zoe?
- Adorable.</i>


00:07:54.732 --> 00:07:57.818
She's changed so much
since you saw her last.


00:07:58.027 --> 00:08:00.446
- Haven't you, sweetheart?
- I don't know.


00:08:00.696 --> 00:08:03.616
<i>- So, what do you guys want for dinner?
- Don't worry about us.</i>


00:08:03.866 --> 00:08:06.952
- We'll just grab a pizza or something.
- I don't think so.


00:08:07.203 --> 00:08:10.247
<i>- So, what does Zoe like these days?
- She eats anything.</i>


00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.917
- She's a vacuum cleaner.
- Mom.


00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:16.128
I'll call you when we get closer.
Say bye to your Aunt Kate.


00:08:16.379 --> 00:08:19.340
- Bye, Aunt Kate.
- Bye, Aunt Kate.


00:08:24.887 --> 00:08:27.765
- Hey, Kate. Did you just get in?
- No, I forgot something.


00:08:27.973 --> 00:08:29.475
- How are you?
- Good.


00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:33.062
Are you working tonight?
I know this great little Thai place.


00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:35.272
Actually, I am.
Just for a couple of hours.


00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.566
My sister's coming into town
with my niece.


00:08:37.733 --> 00:08:40.069
I don't give up that easily.
One of these days...


00:08:40.236 --> 00:08:42.780
...I'm gonna convince you
to have dinner with me.


00:08:42.988 --> 00:08:47.243
Look, Sean, I think you should know
I don't generally do that.


00:08:48.285 --> 00:08:50.788
- What, have dinner?
- Dinner dates.


00:08:51.038 --> 00:08:53.457
- How about breakfast?
- You live in my building.


00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:57.545
I don't generally go out with people
in my building. As a rule.


00:08:58.379 --> 00:09:00.172
You seem to have a lot of rules.


00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:07.555
Didn't you say you forgot something?


00:09:07.763 --> 00:09:10.099
- Oh, thanks. Right.
- You're welcome.


00:09:23.696 --> 00:09:25.781
<i>So, what's the problem
with having rules?</i>


00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:28.951
It's not as if I'm controlling
or anything.


00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.370
I just prefer things
to be done exactly right.


00:09:31.579 --> 00:09:34.457
That's why I usually end up
doing everything myself.


00:09:34.665 --> 00:09:39.545
Do you have any idea how complicated
it is to coordinate 40 dishes at once?


00:09:40.171 --> 00:09:42.048
I hope you like scallops.


00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.760
I thought we agreed you
weren't gonna cook for me anymore.


00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:49.346
I didn't cook it for you,
I just tried some new ideas.


00:09:49.555 --> 00:09:51.640
Who else am I gonna give it to?


00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:55.770
Now, we're gonna try
something new this week.


00:09:56.187 --> 00:10:00.649
I'm going to ask you questions,
and you're gonna answer them.


00:10:00.858 --> 00:10:04.737
How long ago
was your last relationship?


00:10:06.364 --> 00:10:08.616
Isn't that a little personal?


00:10:08.866 --> 00:10:10.326
Well, this is therapy.


00:10:11.035 --> 00:10:12.495
How long?


00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:15.915
I don't know. Three years ago.
Maybe four.


00:10:16.123 --> 00:10:18.751
- Who ended it?
- I did.


00:10:19.001 --> 00:10:22.213
- He was getting way too demanding.
- How so?


00:10:22.755 --> 00:10:27.301
Well, if you must know, after two years
he wanted to move in together.


00:10:27.551 --> 00:10:30.388
Did you try the saffron sauce?


00:10:30.596 --> 00:10:33.933
And, I'm sorry, what's so bad
about moving in together?


00:10:34.558 --> 00:10:37.436
He asked me to give up
my apartment.


00:10:37.645 --> 00:10:39.438
Why would I wanna do that?


00:10:39.647 --> 00:10:41.607
I'd move out,
we'd get a place together...


00:10:41.816 --> 00:10:44.735
...he'd eventually leave,
then where would I be?


00:10:44.944 --> 00:10:46.612
My God.


00:10:47.446 --> 00:10:51.951
- The sauce is so good.
- Thank you.


00:10:55.496 --> 00:10:58.833
- Where's my lobster for table 12?
- Plating, chef.


00:10:59.083 --> 00:11:02.128
I'm an actress
and I don't do naked bondage movies.


00:11:02.336 --> 00:11:06.090
The world is so full of pervs.
That guy at table 10 is the worst.


00:11:06.298 --> 00:11:08.008
Every week a new bimbo.


00:11:08.175 --> 00:11:12.471
I swear, he leers at my tits
one more time, he's gonna regret it.


00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.642
Damn it, Carlos!
Watch where you're going.


00:11:16.851 --> 00:11:18.686
- Pay attention, everybody.
- Sorry, chef.


00:11:18.894 --> 00:11:20.730
Fire two lobsters right away.
Hold the nine.


00:11:20.896 --> 00:11:24.024
- I'm really sorry about that.
- Just don't let it happen again.


00:11:24.233 --> 00:11:26.944
Now you're gonna run out of lobster
right after I leave.


00:11:27.111 --> 00:11:31.490
Kate, we're not gonna run out
of anything, we're fine. Hydrate.


00:11:31.699 --> 00:11:33.200
You're a mom already.


00:11:33.409 --> 00:11:35.661
Well, I've gotta practice
while I can, right?


00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:37.580
- Thanks.
- Thank you.


00:11:42.043 --> 00:11:43.919
Someone get the phone.


00:11:45.963 --> 00:11:48.632
- Kitchen.
- Lf it's my sister, tell her she said 9...


00:11:48.841 --> 00:11:50.468
...can't make it any sooner.


00:11:51.886 --> 00:11:54.305
- It's for you.
- Take a message.


00:11:54.513 --> 00:11:55.848
Kate...


00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:58.434
...I think you better take this.


00:12:01.187 --> 00:12:03.147
- Hello.
- One's done.


00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:05.191
Speaking.


00:12:44.939 --> 00:12:48.692
Ms. Armstrong? I'm Dr. Burton.
We spoke on the phone.


00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:52.780
Zoe's doing great.
She's gonna be fine.


00:12:53.823 --> 00:12:55.282
Has anyone told her yet?


00:12:55.491 --> 00:12:59.203
We thought it would be best for her
to hear it from someone in the family.


00:12:59.412 --> 00:13:01.914
Do you know how
we can reach Zoe's father?


00:13:02.623 --> 00:13:04.583
He's never been...


00:13:06.001 --> 00:13:07.461
I don't even know his name.


00:13:07.628 --> 00:13:10.798
<i>Dr. Burton to Emergency, please.
Paging Dr. Burton...</i>


00:13:10.965 --> 00:13:12.800
I'm so sorry.


00:13:13.843 --> 00:13:17.972
I have to go, but I'll be back to check
on her in just a little bit, okay?


00:13:42.288 --> 00:13:43.748
Hello, Zoe.


00:13:45.332 --> 00:13:46.709
Where's Mom?


00:13:50.129 --> 00:13:51.630
Is she dead?


00:13:55.051 --> 00:13:57.219
She is, isn't she?


00:14:00.723 --> 00:14:02.308
Yes.


00:14:27.041 --> 00:14:30.586
<i>You have one new message.</i>


00:14:31.504 --> 00:14:33.631
<i>- Hi, it's me.
- And me!</i>


00:14:33.839 --> 00:14:35.966
<i>We just wanted you to know
we're running late.</i>


00:14:36.175 --> 00:14:39.637
<i>Traffic's insane.
We'll get there eventually. Bye.</i>


00:14:40.137 --> 00:14:41.847
<i>End of messages.</i>


00:14:50.231 --> 00:14:54.485
Now, this is a beautiful
2002 Dolcetto.


00:14:54.735 --> 00:14:56.362
Any idea where it might be from?


00:14:56.570 --> 00:14:59.699
- Probably Piedmont.
- South Australia. Adelaide Hills.


00:14:59.907 --> 00:15:03.953
If Kate doesn't find a replacement soon,
I'll have this baby behind the stove.


00:15:04.161 --> 00:15:06.580
I think that would be
a health-code violation.


00:15:06.747 --> 00:15:10.418
Bernadette. Look at the color
of this wine. It's absolutely beautiful.


00:15:10.626 --> 00:15:12.586
And it's ready to drink...


00:15:19.927 --> 00:15:23.431
Give me three words
to describe this wine. Three words.


00:15:23.639 --> 00:15:25.683
Did you know she was coming in?


00:15:29.687 --> 00:15:31.647
Kate, what are you doing?


00:15:31.897 --> 00:15:33.190
What do you mean?


00:15:33.441 --> 00:15:35.985
I thought you were gonna take
a few days off.


00:15:36.277 --> 00:15:38.654
- No.
- Are you sure?


00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:40.948
Yeah.


00:15:43.659 --> 00:15:46.537
Give me one duck, two beef rare,
and a rack of lamb.


00:15:46.787 --> 00:15:49.290
I'm still waiting
on those tenderloins of beef.


00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:50.791
Pick up.


00:15:50.958 --> 00:15:54.295
I need a quail and a Dover sole
for table nine. Okay, let's go, guys.


00:15:55.046 --> 00:15:58.049
Come on, let's move it.
Terrine, carpaccio.


00:15:58.299 --> 00:16:00.176
Carlos, I need more pans, pronto.


00:16:00.384 --> 00:16:03.512
- Five minutes on the lobster.
- Cleanup right away on table 13.


00:16:03.679 --> 00:16:06.307
Fire one rare steak on the fly.


00:16:07.058 --> 00:16:09.518
Two duck breast, two rack of lamb.
Let's go, people.


00:16:09.727 --> 00:16:13.064
Why is there no food on the counter?
Come on, we got tables!


00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:16.525
Where's my soufflé for 14?


00:16:22.823 --> 00:16:26.243
<i>Dear Kate, the baby is gorgeous.</i>


00:16:27.536 --> 00:16:31.082
<i>I've called her Zoe,
which means "life. "</i>


00:16:31.499 --> 00:16:34.210
<i>Now she's here, I'm beginning
to get what a huge thing...</i>


00:16:34.418 --> 00:16:36.253
<i>...it is I'm doing on my own.</i>


00:16:36.462 --> 00:16:40.049
<i>So I want you to know
if anything should ever happen to me...</i>


00:16:40.257 --> 00:16:43.677
<i>...you are the only person
I would want to have her.</i>


00:16:43.969 --> 00:16:47.932
<i>I know you'll love my baby
the same way I would.</i>


00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:52.019
<i>Listen to me,
it must be the three-day blues.</i>


00:16:52.395 --> 00:16:55.689
<i>I love you, sis. Christine.</i>


00:17:10.454 --> 00:17:11.747
Kate...


00:17:13.541 --> 00:17:15.960
...I want you to take a week off.


00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:19.505
That's not a suggestion, it's an order.


00:17:31.434 --> 00:17:33.185
<i>What's up, Doc?</i>


00:17:33.436 --> 00:17:37.940
<i>Allow me to introduce myself.
My name is Wile E. Coyote, genius.</i>


00:17:38.107 --> 00:17:39.358
Hello, Zoe.


00:17:39.567 --> 00:17:42.570
<i>I'm sorry, Mac, the lady of the house
ain't home and besides...</i>


00:17:42.778 --> 00:17:44.905
<i>...we mailed your refund check
last week.</i>


00:17:45.281 --> 00:17:47.199
I cooked us something tasty.


00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.243
I'm not hungry.


00:17:50.494 --> 00:17:52.121
Okay.


00:18:02.173 --> 00:18:05.468
You know, you can leave on Friday.
You know that?


00:18:05.676 --> 00:18:07.136
Yes.


00:18:13.517 --> 00:18:16.812
Zoe, you and I have to talk
about what's gonna happen.


00:18:17.229 --> 00:18:18.647
Can I go back home?


00:18:20.483 --> 00:18:22.360
I'm afraid not.


00:18:23.027 --> 00:18:24.653
Why not?


00:18:26.405 --> 00:18:28.866
Well, you'd be alone there.


00:18:31.118 --> 00:18:33.371
Your mom asked me
to take care of you.


00:18:34.997 --> 00:18:36.832
So you'll be coming home
with me, okay?


00:19:12.868 --> 00:19:15.830
So the kitchen
is just to the right there.


00:19:16.664 --> 00:19:18.082
The living room.


00:19:20.292 --> 00:19:23.212
This is my bedroom and the bathroom.


00:19:24.964 --> 00:19:26.298
This will be your bedroom.


00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:04.587
<i>We'll have sunshine today.
It's cold, a high of 36.</i>


00:20:07.965 --> 00:20:12.011
Her name is Nelly. I've had her
since I was 3. She has a whole family.


00:20:13.137 --> 00:20:15.639
You should see all my other animals.


00:20:20.519 --> 00:20:22.980
Zoe, dinner's ready!


00:20:23.189 --> 00:20:24.648
Okay.


00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:30.988
<i>Bon appétit.</i>


00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:39.205
Everything all right?


00:20:40.831 --> 00:20:44.001
What's the matter?
Aren't you hungry?


00:20:46.045 --> 00:20:47.922
Can I go back to my room?


00:20:49.382 --> 00:20:50.591
Sure.


00:21:05.606 --> 00:21:08.609
Zoe, I have to stop by the restaurant
for a couple of minutes.


00:21:08.859 --> 00:21:11.404
Will you be okay here on your own
for a little while?


00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:13.239
- Yes.
- Now, if you need me...


00:21:13.447 --> 00:21:17.952
...just press one, that's my cell phone,
and two, that's the restaurant, okay?


00:21:18.202 --> 00:21:22.248
It's only a few blocks away, so if you
need me I can be back here in no time.


00:21:22.456 --> 00:21:25.126
- All right?
- Okay.


00:21:25.835 --> 00:21:27.420
I won't be long.


00:22:04.123 --> 00:22:05.666
Hi, Kate.


00:22:11.547 --> 00:22:13.799
He says, "Look! Look at the stars!


00:22:14.425 --> 00:22:17.553
Gaze at the stars which tremble
with love. "


00:22:17.762 --> 00:22:19.430
Hello, chef.


00:22:20.556 --> 00:22:22.058
Oh, my God, it's you.


00:22:22.641 --> 00:22:26.312
I am begging you, will you please tell me
the secret of your saffron sauce?


00:22:27.188 --> 00:22:28.481
Excuse me?


00:22:29.732 --> 00:22:32.234
Listen to this, guys.
Listen to this right here.


00:22:33.486 --> 00:22:35.071
Listen.


00:22:35.821 --> 00:22:39.742
He's saying, "Fade the stars,
fade all the stars. "


00:22:46.248 --> 00:22:48.167
So you guys are my string section.


00:22:48.834 --> 00:22:51.837
He says, "In the morning
I am going to wake. "


00:22:55.341 --> 00:22:57.259
"This is our love. "


00:22:59.553 --> 00:23:02.181
Now, everybody. "Win our love. "


00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:20.700
All right, all right. Back to work!


00:23:23.035 --> 00:23:24.912
Who do you think you are?


00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:27.748
Nicholas Palmer.


00:23:27.998 --> 00:23:32.753
And may I just say the world
would be a dark and depressing place...


00:23:33.003 --> 00:23:35.423
...without your quail in truffle sauce.


00:23:37.633 --> 00:23:39.093
We need to talk.


00:23:40.553 --> 00:23:43.431
- You could've at least asked me.
- I'm sorry. I couldn't wait.


00:23:43.639 --> 00:23:46.392
Nick became available.
I had to act quickly.


00:23:46.559 --> 00:23:49.562
The last thing I need right now
is some lunatic in my kitchen.


00:23:49.770 --> 00:23:53.441
He's not a lunatic. He's exuberant. God
knows we could use that around here.


00:23:53.649 --> 00:23:56.944
Exuberant? Are you kidding me?
The guy thinks he's Pavarotti.


00:23:57.153 --> 00:23:59.113
Good evening.
Do you have a reservation?


00:23:59.321 --> 00:24:01.574
- Yes, Matthews.
- Matthews. Yes.


00:24:01.782 --> 00:24:03.909
May I take your coats, please?


00:24:05.411 --> 00:24:08.831
Let me show you to your table.
Excuse me.


00:24:10.624 --> 00:24:12.334
Your waiter will be right over.


00:24:12.543 --> 00:24:15.046
The only demand I had
when I took this position...


00:24:15.212 --> 00:24:17.089
...was I get to choose
who I work with.


00:24:17.298 --> 00:24:20.509
- Leah would have been just fine.
- Leah can barely stand up anymore.


00:24:20.718 --> 00:24:23.054
If I push her, she's gonna fall over.


00:24:28.559 --> 00:24:31.854
Holding her crotch and chopping
at the same time! Give him a chance.


00:24:32.021 --> 00:24:34.190
- Nick is excellent.
- I know nothing about him.


00:24:34.356 --> 00:24:36.442
- I have no idea what...
- Give me some credit.


00:24:36.609 --> 00:24:39.195
- He was the sous-chef at II Treviso.
- Italian?


00:24:39.403 --> 00:24:43.699
You bring a sous-chef from an Italian
restaurant, and I'm the one in therapy?


00:24:44.241 --> 00:24:47.203
We were lucky to get him.
Peninsula offered him executive chef.


00:24:47.453 --> 00:24:48.579
Why didn't he take it?


00:24:48.788 --> 00:24:51.415
Because he said he wanted
to work with you.


00:25:33.165 --> 00:25:34.542
Zoe.


00:25:42.425 --> 00:25:46.220
<i>Funny thing to me about being in these
cabs is when you're in Manhattan...</i>


00:25:46.429 --> 00:25:50.057
<i>...for some reason you don't get scared
no matter how fast you're going.</i>


00:25:50.266 --> 00:25:55.438
<i>Well, you know, he's driving fast
and recklessly. He's a professional.</i>


00:25:56.731 --> 00:26:00.234
<i>He's got a cab-driver's license,
I can see it right there.</i>


00:26:00.401 --> 00:26:03.404
<i>I don't even know what it takes
to get a cab-driver's license.</i>


00:26:03.612 --> 00:26:05.740
<i>I think all you need is a face.</i>


00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:10.578
<i>This seems to be
their big qualification.</i>


00:26:10.786 --> 00:26:14.248
<i>No blank heads are allowed
driving cabs in this town.</i>


00:27:24.068 --> 00:27:27.405
Kate, wake up.


00:27:30.074 --> 00:27:31.534
Kate.


00:27:32.368 --> 00:27:34.203
School starts at 9.


00:27:35.913 --> 00:27:37.415
It's 8:20.


00:27:44.463 --> 00:27:46.173
Oh, no.


00:27:46.841 --> 00:27:51.095
Oh, jeez. Okay, let's get dressed,
come on. Oh, you're dressed.


00:27:51.345 --> 00:27:53.013
Okay, okay, one minute.


00:27:54.056 --> 00:27:57.143
Do you need supplies or anything?
Like pens or paper?


00:27:57.393 --> 00:27:59.061
They usually have those things.


00:28:00.146 --> 00:28:04.358
I made your lunch yesterday.
I hope you like duck.


00:28:06.235 --> 00:28:07.862
Okay, come on! Let's go.


00:28:08.571 --> 00:28:11.115
- I can't find my scarf.
- Don't worry about it.


00:28:11.365 --> 00:28:14.285
I can't have you late for your
first day of school. Let's go.


00:28:14.452 --> 00:28:16.746
- I need my scarf.
- Zoe, just use one of mine.


00:28:16.912 --> 00:28:18.914
We'll find yours later, all right?


00:28:22.126 --> 00:28:24.128
Let's go find your scarf.


00:28:29.633 --> 00:28:31.427
Here it is.


00:28:34.513 --> 00:28:36.265
Is this it?


00:28:42.313 --> 00:28:45.191
- That's it.
- Great.


00:28:46.317 --> 00:28:47.526
That was easy.


00:28:49.028 --> 00:28:50.279
Let's go.


00:28:52.656 --> 00:28:54.408
Okay.


00:28:56.369 --> 00:28:57.995
Your lunch.


00:28:59.538 --> 00:29:01.415
Could you get that, please?


00:29:07.880 --> 00:29:09.340
Why didn't you get the door?


00:29:09.548 --> 00:29:12.009
I'm not supposed to answer
the door for strangers.


00:29:12.218 --> 00:29:15.179
Right. Yeah, that's smart.


00:29:15.429 --> 00:29:17.515
- Hi, Sean.
- Any chance for some coffee?


00:29:17.723 --> 00:29:20.851
- I've just run out.
- Sure. We're running a little late but...


00:29:21.060 --> 00:29:23.145
Just one second.


00:29:23.354 --> 00:29:26.565
Good morning. I'm Sean.
I live downstairs.


00:29:28.109 --> 00:29:29.819
You must be Kate's niece.


00:29:30.820 --> 00:29:32.071
Zoe, right?


00:29:39.412 --> 00:29:41.247
My kids are about your age.


00:29:42.623 --> 00:29:46.210
They'll be staying with me this weekend.
Are you gonna be around?


00:29:48.879 --> 00:29:50.089
Here you go.


00:29:50.297 --> 00:29:51.966
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.


00:29:52.174 --> 00:29:54.009
- The good stuff.
- Yeah.


00:29:54.719 --> 00:29:57.847
All right, let's go.


00:29:58.180 --> 00:29:59.223
Quickly.


00:29:59.390 --> 00:30:01.392
Thank you
for the Thai noodles last night.


00:30:01.559 --> 00:30:03.269
- No problem.
- That was really nice.


00:30:14.572 --> 00:30:18.409
- I guess this is where you go in, right?
- I don't know.


00:30:18.617 --> 00:30:21.078
Right. Come on.


00:30:27.460 --> 00:30:29.170
It's gonna be fine.


00:30:29.420 --> 00:30:32.131
Ms. Armstrong?
I'm Ellen Parker, the principal.


00:30:32.339 --> 00:30:34.050
- Kate.
- You must be Zoe.


00:30:34.258 --> 00:30:36.052
- Very nice to meet you.
- Hello.


00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:39.555
I'll take you to the classroom
and we'll meet your teacher.


00:30:44.602 --> 00:30:46.812
<i>There has to be someone
better suited for this.</i>


00:30:47.438 --> 00:30:51.692
I have no idea what to do with a kid,
especially one who's lost her mother.


00:30:51.942 --> 00:30:53.944
How do their minds work?


00:30:54.153 --> 00:30:57.073
I can't get Zoe to eat anything I make.


00:30:57.281 --> 00:31:01.619
- What am I supposed to do, force her?
- Maybe she misses her mother's cooking.


00:31:01.827 --> 00:31:03.788
My sister never cooked.


00:31:04.663 --> 00:31:06.957
- She reheated.
- Well, that's the point.


00:31:07.166 --> 00:31:12.630
Maybe Zoe needs something
more familiar, less sophisticated.


00:31:12.838 --> 00:31:14.632
What did you eat
when you were a kid?


00:31:15.174 --> 00:31:18.386
- It's not the same.
- What do you mean?


00:31:19.178 --> 00:31:20.971
My mother was an amazing cook.


00:31:21.180 --> 00:31:23.516
Of course, I was the only one
who appreciated it.


00:31:23.682 --> 00:31:28.020
And after your mother passed away,
did your father take over the cooking?


00:31:28.229 --> 00:31:31.732
No. He didn't take over anything.


00:31:32.733 --> 00:31:35.653
We were lucky if we even saw him
at dinner.


00:31:36.195 --> 00:31:40.700
- So who took care of the two of you?
- Can we not get into this right now?


00:31:41.575 --> 00:31:43.119
Okay.


00:31:45.705 --> 00:31:48.416
What about fish sticks?
Kids love them.


00:31:49.500 --> 00:31:51.335
Fish sticks?


00:31:51.502 --> 00:31:53.754
Yeah, you know, they're frozen
and breaded...


00:31:53.921 --> 00:31:55.756
I know what fish sticks are.


00:31:56.882 --> 00:31:59.760
I just can't believe I'm paying
for these suggestions.


00:32:01.512 --> 00:32:03.055
Fish sticks.


00:32:22.867 --> 00:32:26.871
- Did you learn anything interesting?
- No.


00:32:28.581 --> 00:32:32.293
- Anything uninteresting?
- No.


00:32:33.461 --> 00:32:35.296
- How was your teacher?
- Bald.


00:32:36.756 --> 00:32:38.591
Well, that's interesting.


00:32:42.303 --> 00:32:44.221
Fish sticks.


00:32:44.889 --> 00:32:49.268
You know, I was thinking the other day,
I know so little about you.


00:32:49.477 --> 00:32:53.731
I mean, we're family, but I don't
even know what your favorite color is.


00:32:53.898 --> 00:32:58.235
- Red.
- Red? See, I didn't know that.


00:32:58.444 --> 00:33:01.572
I love red. Red's a great color.


00:33:03.449 --> 00:33:07.286
- What's your favorite number?
- You know, you don't have to do this.


00:33:08.829 --> 00:33:09.955
Do what?


00:33:10.873 --> 00:33:12.124
Try so hard.


00:33:20.174 --> 00:33:21.759
Coming!


00:33:23.761 --> 00:33:25.304
Hi, I'm Charlotte.


00:33:27.640 --> 00:33:31.519
- From the agency?
- You expecting another Charlotte?


00:33:36.357 --> 00:33:37.400
No.


00:33:41.362 --> 00:33:42.988
So can I come in or what?


00:33:43.698 --> 00:33:45.908
Oh, sure. Come on in.


00:33:50.705 --> 00:33:52.665
Excuse me one second.


00:33:56.043 --> 00:33:59.046
I told you, I don't need a babysitter.
I'm not a baby anymore.


00:33:59.296 --> 00:34:02.341
So, what am I supposed to do?
I can't leave you here alone.


00:34:02.508 --> 00:34:04.009
Why not? I'm perfectly fine.


00:34:04.176 --> 00:34:06.887
Zoe, you barricaded the door,
remember?


00:34:07.513 --> 00:34:10.224
I charge from when I get here,
you know.


00:34:10.433 --> 00:34:12.059
Yeah.


00:34:12.309 --> 00:34:14.729
I see you've brought
something to read to Zoe.


00:34:14.937 --> 00:34:16.230
It's for my thesis.


00:34:16.439 --> 00:34:21.235
Rapidly mutating deadly viruses.
You know, like Ebola, that sort of thing.


00:34:26.115 --> 00:34:29.035
Well, have fun at work.


00:34:31.704 --> 00:34:34.206
22 Bleecker, can I help you?


00:34:35.416 --> 00:34:38.961
Table for five?
Yes, I can seat you at 9.


00:34:39.211 --> 00:34:41.964
- I know.
- Yes.


00:34:44.508 --> 00:34:46.761
How do you want the sea bass
prepared tonight?


00:34:46.969 --> 00:34:50.389
Tell them they're gonna be served
to some very important people.


00:34:54.769 --> 00:34:57.938
- You don't like music?
- It's distracting my staff.


00:34:58.147 --> 00:35:02.026
Nick, you were right.
Pavarotti makes sex so much better.


00:35:02.234 --> 00:35:06.697
Glad to hear it. Bocelli's good too,
but only for shallow one-night stands.


00:35:10.409 --> 00:35:12.411
Pronto. Food. Belly. Now.


00:35:13.913 --> 00:35:15.956
Thank you. Thank you.


00:35:17.833 --> 00:35:22.004
Me plus baby
equals extra large portions, please.


00:35:25.800 --> 00:35:28.677
Bernadette. Bernadette.


00:35:29.011 --> 00:35:30.096
That's it.


00:35:31.430 --> 00:35:34.642
David, Richard.
It's gonna be, I think, all men.


00:35:35.184 --> 00:35:36.560
I think I can handle it.


00:35:36.811 --> 00:35:37.937
Good luck.


00:35:38.145 --> 00:35:39.522
John.


00:35:40.815 --> 00:35:43.693
- Chef.
- No, thank you.


00:35:43.984 --> 00:35:45.444
Delicious, chef.


00:35:49.532 --> 00:35:53.035
Only a full cook can judge food.
When you're hungry, everything tastes...


00:35:53.244 --> 00:35:56.372
...better than it really is.
- I never eat in the afternoon.


00:36:07.341 --> 00:36:12.263
My grandmother whispered this recipe
into my ear on her deathbed.


00:36:12.513 --> 00:36:18.185
She brought it over from the Old Country
and I made it especially for you today.


00:36:33.242 --> 00:36:35.703
- Happy?
- Very happy.


00:36:39.623 --> 00:36:42.251
I thought your grandmother
lived in Miami.


00:36:42.793 --> 00:36:44.378
Well, you know...


00:36:46.380 --> 00:36:51.052
Well, we all thought she wasn't
gonna make it. It was like a miracle.


00:36:57.808 --> 00:36:59.810
It was a miracle.


00:37:02.296 --> 00:37:05.049
You take care of those dishes
and I'll take care of these.


00:37:05.299 --> 00:37:09.220
- Then we won't get in each other's way.
- Wait, your half is bigger than mine.


00:37:09.428 --> 00:37:11.055
Right, right, right.


00:37:11.222 --> 00:37:12.807
I have some very big items.


00:37:13.015 --> 00:37:16.727
I got beef, I got fish, I got rabbit.


00:37:16.978 --> 00:37:19.230
Showtime, folks! Let's go.


00:37:24.402 --> 00:37:27.697
Fifteen, two terrines,
one Dover sole, two lamb.


00:37:27.905 --> 00:37:30.283
Seven, carpaccio.


00:37:32.034 --> 00:37:34.203
- Have you seasoned that right?
- Yes, chef.


00:37:39.333 --> 00:37:40.543
It's okay.


00:38:02.356 --> 00:38:06.527
- Okay, where am I? Where's my lamb?
- Slicing it now.


00:38:07.236 --> 00:38:08.863
One second. One second.


00:38:47.385 --> 00:38:48.678
- Pardon me.
- I need that.


00:38:48.845 --> 00:38:50.513
And you'll get it right back.


00:38:55.852 --> 00:38:58.980
- Can I ask you something?
- Do I have a choice?


00:39:00.356 --> 00:39:02.358
Where did you learn to cook so well?


00:39:04.402 --> 00:39:05.695
My mother.


00:39:05.862 --> 00:39:08.406
Seriously? I thought
you were gonna say you studied...


00:39:08.573 --> 00:39:11.075
...under Alain Passard at L'Arpège
or something.


00:39:12.118 --> 00:39:16.247
I did. But my mom was better,
and she didn't throw plates at me.


00:39:29.635 --> 00:39:33.264
Oh, God. I need more space.


00:39:42.732 --> 00:39:44.984
- Why are you so mad at me?
- I'm not mad at you.


00:39:45.943 --> 00:39:47.403
You're very mad.


00:39:47.612 --> 00:39:50.907
Look, this is my kitchen.
I've worked really hard to get here...


00:39:51.115 --> 00:39:53.576
...and I'm not gonna let you
take it away from me.


00:39:55.453 --> 00:39:57.455
What makes you think
I wanna take it away?


00:39:57.663 --> 00:39:59.999
What else could you possibly want?


00:40:02.835 --> 00:40:04.712
<i>You treat me like a dog, Larry.</i>


00:40:05.004 --> 00:40:09.509
I'm not a dog. I'm a human being!
A human being, goddamn...


00:40:10.051 --> 00:40:12.428
I'm sorry, I have an audition.


00:40:12.637 --> 00:40:14.180
Would you mind?


00:40:29.362 --> 00:40:32.615
Look, I don't need this job.
I can work wherever I want.


00:40:32.824 --> 00:40:36.702
I'd like to work here because
it's an honor to cook with you...


00:40:36.911 --> 00:40:39.747
...but I'd rather work
somewhere I'm welcome.


00:40:39.956 --> 00:40:43.793
So if you want me to go,
you just say the word.


00:40:46.045 --> 00:40:48.381
Want to tell me
what's going on in here?


00:40:49.131 --> 00:40:50.466
Well?


00:40:54.387 --> 00:40:56.347
Wait a minute, where are you going?


00:40:56.514 --> 00:40:58.641
I'm sorry,
you'll have to find someone else.


00:40:58.850 --> 00:41:01.561
- Kate, what have you done?
- I didn't do anything.


00:41:02.687 --> 00:41:05.064
Nick, please. We need you.


00:41:05.273 --> 00:41:07.567
Well, I'll have to hear that from her.


00:41:07.859 --> 00:41:09.652
It's my restaurant.


00:41:09.861 --> 00:41:12.530
It may be your restaurant, Paula,
but it's her kitchen.


00:41:13.156 --> 00:41:14.866
Without her...


00:41:15.575 --> 00:41:19.871
...all this would just be a pile
of hot metal and dirty dishes, so...


00:41:20.788 --> 00:41:22.415
She decides.


00:41:23.207 --> 00:41:24.584
Kate.


00:41:31.282 --> 00:41:32.992
Seems you've left me no choice.


00:41:34.494 --> 00:41:38.081
- Do you want me to stay?
- Didn't I just say that?


00:41:39.665 --> 00:41:41.000
I didn't hear those words.


00:41:42.460 --> 00:41:45.463
I want you to stay.


00:41:45.671 --> 00:41:48.841
Love to. Thought you'd never ask.


00:41:51.052 --> 00:41:52.804
You're on fire.


00:42:28.673 --> 00:42:32.593
And I know you guys are scared,
but it's okay, because I'm here.


00:42:32.802 --> 00:42:37.348
But if you get really scared, you can
wake me up and I'll hold your hand.


00:42:37.557 --> 00:42:40.601
Especially you, Louie,
because you're the littlest.


00:42:40.810 --> 00:42:42.145
Zoe?


00:42:42.770 --> 00:42:44.272
Hi.


00:42:47.066 --> 00:42:49.360
When did Charlotte leave?


00:42:49.569 --> 00:42:52.071
I don't know. A while ago.


00:42:57.910 --> 00:42:59.954
Looks so cozy in there.


00:43:09.589 --> 00:43:11.215
I have an idea.


00:43:13.051 --> 00:43:18.347
How about you come with me
to the restaurant tomorrow night?


00:43:29.317 --> 00:43:30.818
Night.


00:43:31.652 --> 00:43:32.945
Night.


00:44:05.019 --> 00:44:06.521
Please.


00:44:17.657 --> 00:44:22.036
I've tried everything. No matter
what I make, she doesn't eat it.


00:44:22.203 --> 00:44:24.914
Why not try giving her
some regular kid food?


00:44:25.540 --> 00:44:28.084
Have you been talking to my therapist?


00:44:32.296 --> 00:44:37.385
All right, two foie gras, one tartare,
two bisque and a goat cheese.


00:44:51.399 --> 00:44:52.900
Breathe in.


00:44:54.819 --> 00:44:55.903
<i>It's basilico.</i>


00:45:12.545 --> 00:45:17.091
Kate. Kate, your biggest fans
are dying to see you.


00:45:25.099 --> 00:45:27.894
Leah, finish the duck on table five?
I gotta take a break.


00:45:28.102 --> 00:45:29.562
Yeah, sure.


00:45:44.452 --> 00:45:49.290
All right, I need one terrine, two bisque
and a langoustine, please.


00:45:58.549 --> 00:45:59.675
Good.


00:46:03.471 --> 00:46:06.224
Table 12's getting a little antsy.
Will it be up soon?


00:46:08.017 --> 00:46:09.310
Hold this.


00:46:18.986 --> 00:46:21.823
Fire one duck,
one sea bass and a soufflé, please.


00:46:33.584 --> 00:46:35.253
It's working now, chef.


00:46:35.711 --> 00:46:38.673
Table five's coming up
in a few seconds, chef.


00:46:39.507 --> 00:46:41.008
Save some for me.


00:46:43.261 --> 00:46:44.679
You know, in ancient Rome...


00:46:45.221 --> 00:46:48.766
...guys used to chew basil
before the prom to get rid of bad breath.


00:46:49.392 --> 00:46:50.768
It's true.


00:47:08.119 --> 00:47:09.370
<i>Thank you.</i>


00:47:13.499 --> 00:47:18.087
- They didn't have proms in ancient Rome.
- They didn't? Are you sure?


00:47:20.965 --> 00:47:22.592
I thought they did.


00:47:31.559 --> 00:47:34.479
- See you tomorrow.
- Thanks, Leah.


00:47:54.373 --> 00:47:56.709
- Good night.
- Good night.


00:48:47.176 --> 00:48:49.053
Where are you going?


00:48:58.229 --> 00:49:00.857
- Hi, Bob.
- Hi, Kate. How you doing?


00:49:01.065 --> 00:49:03.151
- Good. What you got?
- I got fresh bluefin.


00:49:03.359 --> 00:49:07.196
Just came in like five minutes ago.
I got baby mollusks over there.


00:49:07.405 --> 00:49:09.240
What's behind you there?


00:49:09.449 --> 00:49:12.076
- Colorados.
- Yeah, I'm gonna take some of those.


00:49:12.285 --> 00:49:14.746
Unbelievably fresh. Look at this.


00:49:20.752 --> 00:49:23.546
<i>Good morning, it's 24 degrees,
sunny at 9:00...</i>


00:49:23.755 --> 00:49:25.923
<i>...on this Tuesday, February 28th.</i>


00:49:29.594 --> 00:49:31.137
Zoe.


00:49:31.304 --> 00:49:32.722
Zoe. Zoe. Zoe.


00:49:32.889 --> 00:49:34.223
Wake up.


00:49:34.390 --> 00:49:38.394
You're gonna be late for school. Here are
your boots. Come on. Let's go, let's go.


00:49:42.899 --> 00:49:45.401
Just tell them it was my fault, okay?


00:49:55.787 --> 00:49:59.123
Ladies, you are very lucky today.
I have new shipment.


00:49:59.332 --> 00:50:03.461
They are from all over the place.
Modena, Montferrato, Bologna.


00:50:03.669 --> 00:50:06.297
Big sniff.
It's a black truffle from Parma.


00:50:06.506 --> 00:50:07.715
It's not bad.


00:50:09.092 --> 00:50:12.261
- What do you have in white?
- My best product.


00:50:12.470 --> 00:50:15.723
Very, very hard
to find this time of year.


00:50:19.394 --> 00:50:22.814
- Who'd you get them from?
- You know I never reveal my sources.


00:50:23.272 --> 00:50:25.942
- So how much for the white?
- Twenty-two hundred a pound.


00:50:26.150 --> 00:50:28.611
- Oh, my God.
- They are from Alba.


00:50:28.820 --> 00:50:31.489
No, no, no.
I think my water just broke.


00:50:31.697 --> 00:50:34.158
- What? You're kidding me.
- No, I'm not kidding you.


00:50:34.325 --> 00:50:37.161
- Oh, my God. Are you okay?
- I don't know.


00:50:37.370 --> 00:50:39.747
- Can you call 911?
- No, no, no. No police.


00:50:39.956 --> 00:50:43.459
It's not the police. We need
an ambulance, she's having a baby.


00:50:43.668 --> 00:50:46.587
Oh, my God.
Okay, just keep relaxed.


00:50:46.796 --> 00:50:49.382
We have pregnant lady,
Bleecker and Charles.


00:50:49.590 --> 00:50:52.385
22 Bleecker Street.
Her water just broke.


00:50:52.593 --> 00:50:55.638
- 22 Bleecker on the corner of Charles.
- Bernadette!


00:50:55.847 --> 00:50:57.557
Okay, thank you.


00:50:57.807 --> 00:50:59.726
Breathe, yes.


00:51:03.104 --> 00:51:04.480
Breathe.


00:51:21.414 --> 00:51:22.915
Oh, no!


00:51:30.840 --> 00:51:35.428
Just on the left. You see the steps?
Here. Stop! Stop! Just wait.


00:51:42.060 --> 00:51:43.394
Oh, Zoe.


00:51:44.729 --> 00:51:46.689
- I'm so sorry.
- You forgot me.


00:51:46.939 --> 00:51:49.233
- It's not what you think.
- You forgot me.


00:51:49.442 --> 00:51:51.944
Leah had her baby,
I had to take her to the hospital.


00:51:52.153 --> 00:51:53.613
But you still forgot me.


00:51:54.447 --> 00:51:57.450
Okay, I forgot you.


00:51:58.284 --> 00:51:59.368
And I'm so sorry.


00:52:02.288 --> 00:52:05.416
Come on, Zoe. Let's go home.


00:52:07.460 --> 00:52:09.921
Zoe, come on, it's freezing out here.


00:52:11.130 --> 00:52:13.383
Zoe. Move it!


00:52:51.604 --> 00:52:55.150
Zoe, I'm sorry. I totally blew it.


00:52:55.400 --> 00:52:57.360
I know I'm doing everything wrong.


00:52:58.945 --> 00:53:01.406
But I'm doing my best, okay?


00:53:08.038 --> 00:53:11.583
Why don't you think of something
I can do to make it up to you?


00:53:14.210 --> 00:53:16.504
You mean like a wish?


00:53:16.921 --> 00:53:18.214
Yeah.


00:53:18.631 --> 00:53:22.010
Yeah, you wish for something
and I try and make it happen.


00:53:22.218 --> 00:53:26.222
And in return, you forgive me.


00:53:31.436 --> 00:53:34.356
- Can I save it for later?
- Sure.


00:53:40.070 --> 00:53:41.446
Kate...


00:53:42.656 --> 00:53:44.741
...you're not doing everything wrong.


00:54:39.796 --> 00:54:41.381
Really expensive.


00:54:46.511 --> 00:54:50.640
All over the kitchen, everybody knows
about it. Carrots are a different matter.


00:55:18.710 --> 00:55:21.171
Here you go. How many left?


00:55:54.913 --> 00:55:56.539
- Kate?
- Yeah?


00:55:57.666 --> 00:56:00.251
- You're not working tomorrow, are you?
- Nope.


00:56:00.835 --> 00:56:04.005
And Nick
isn't working tomorrow, is he?


00:56:05.215 --> 00:56:06.716
Sunday, we're closed.


00:56:07.676 --> 00:56:09.135
Why?


00:56:18.895 --> 00:56:20.730
Why's that?


00:56:21.564 --> 00:56:22.899
It's my wish.


00:56:27.028 --> 00:56:28.530
<i>It was Zoe's idea, not mine.</i>


00:56:29.656 --> 00:56:32.742
- How come I knew that?
- She says she prefers Italian.


00:56:32.909 --> 00:56:35.787
- Your kitchen or mine?
- Wouldn't it be easier to do it here?


00:56:36.037 --> 00:56:38.707
- Fine, we'll use mine.
- But my kitchen's fully equipped.


00:56:38.915 --> 00:56:41.793
Perfect. Shall we say noon?
I'll do the shopping.


00:56:56.391 --> 00:56:59.311
- Aren't you cold?
- He's late.


00:57:01.062 --> 00:57:02.439
Men.


00:57:08.737 --> 00:57:10.071
I'll be right there.


00:57:10.280 --> 00:57:12.490
<i>- Hello?
- Help.</i>


00:57:12.741 --> 00:57:14.284
Coming!


00:57:19.622 --> 00:57:21.708
- Hey, you.
- You need a hand?


00:57:21.916 --> 00:57:23.293
No, I got it.


00:57:24.336 --> 00:57:26.338
This way. I'll get that.


00:57:26.546 --> 00:57:27.964
Afternoon, chef.


00:57:28.173 --> 00:57:30.592
Got the goodies. Where's the kitchen?


00:57:30.800 --> 00:57:34.137
Right there.
Yeah, yeah, right. Okay, Yeah.


00:57:38.308 --> 00:57:40.727
Okay, sous-chef, put on your apron.


00:57:42.312 --> 00:57:46.358
- Now, do you have a cast-iron pan?
- Of course I have a cast-iron pan.


00:57:47.150 --> 00:57:48.526
Good.


00:57:52.822 --> 00:57:55.867
No, no, no.
Don't touch my Tupperware.


00:57:57.118 --> 00:58:01.748
Tonight, Zoe and I make dinner,
and only Zoe and I. Zoe.


00:58:01.956 --> 00:58:04.834
- But I could help.
- But it's my wish.


00:58:08.004 --> 00:58:09.923
Tonight we're making pizza.


00:58:12.342 --> 00:58:14.469
- Pizza pans, please, sous-chef.
- Okay.


00:58:15.512 --> 00:58:19.099
Gotta get the flour, little eggs,
we'll roll some dough, okay?


00:58:19.474 --> 00:58:22.310
Work your hands in there.
That's good.


00:58:24.020 --> 00:58:26.231
Get your fingers in there.
Just like that.


00:58:26.439 --> 00:58:29.985
You create your own person and buy
them pets but you have to make enough.


00:58:30.193 --> 00:58:31.653
Nice and round.


00:58:31.861 --> 00:58:34.739
Then when you're ready, go like that,
then you go like that.


00:58:34.948 --> 00:58:38.702
That was the first thing he taught me.
Both hands. Gotta know how to do it.


00:58:39.703 --> 00:58:41.454
That's what drapes over.


00:58:42.080 --> 00:58:45.875
Right? Yeah, good,
and then just go like that.


00:58:47.752 --> 00:58:50.547
<i>Then you gotta sing Italiano.
You go like that.</i>


00:58:51.256 --> 00:58:53.425
Then you slap it down like that.


00:58:53.925 --> 00:58:56.928
Remember what I told you.
You can do it.


00:59:00.223 --> 00:59:01.933
Kate! We're ready.


00:59:04.644 --> 00:59:06.062
No shoes.


00:59:06.896 --> 00:59:08.106
Okay.


00:59:11.067 --> 00:59:13.111
Close your eyes. Come with me.


00:59:15.447 --> 00:59:18.408
- What's the secret?
- You'll see.


00:59:19.075 --> 00:59:20.410
No peeking.


00:59:21.619 --> 00:59:22.620
Almost there.


00:59:26.666 --> 00:59:28.752
Okay, open your eyes.


00:59:29.002 --> 00:59:30.295
Surprise.


00:59:32.088 --> 00:59:33.882
I guess we're not eating
at the table.


00:59:34.090 --> 00:59:36.509
We don't have one. We're on safari.


00:59:36.760 --> 00:59:38.178
I see.


00:59:39.387 --> 00:59:42.474
- You forgot the plates.
- No, no. Sit down. We don't need plates.


00:59:42.682 --> 00:59:44.017
- No plates?
- No plates.


00:59:44.184 --> 00:59:46.186
Dirty plates attract the big cats.


00:59:46.436 --> 00:59:48.647
Well, we certainly
don't want the big cats.


00:59:50.440 --> 00:59:52.442
Let me guess who made the pizza.


00:59:52.651 --> 00:59:55.195
- Me! Me. Me, me, me.
- Really?


01:00:08.458 --> 01:00:10.543
Whose idea, though? Your idea.


01:00:10.752 --> 01:00:12.587
Yours has the tusks on it.


01:00:20.011 --> 01:00:22.639
Oh, you were so close.


01:00:31.481 --> 01:00:32.607
Nothing moved.


01:00:32.816 --> 01:00:35.026
But I get my eye poked out. That's okay.


01:00:50.792 --> 01:00:53.837
It's a vampire. It's a king turtle.


01:00:55.797 --> 01:00:57.716
<i>The king, The Lion King!</i>


01:00:57.924 --> 01:00:59.384
Yes! Yes!


01:01:07.767 --> 01:01:09.269
I should put her to bed.


01:01:09.519 --> 01:01:10.770
Allow me.


01:01:11.563 --> 01:01:13.064
Thank you.


01:01:41.968 --> 01:01:44.554
So where did you go
to cooking school?


01:01:44.971 --> 01:01:47.474
As a young child, I sat
at my grandmother's knee...


01:01:47.682 --> 01:01:49.851
Oh, yeah, in Miami, right.


01:01:50.143 --> 01:01:54.105
It was in Pittsburgh, actually.
My father was a steelworker.


01:01:54.648 --> 01:01:56.608
But you did go to cooking school?


01:01:56.858 --> 01:01:59.778
Are you kidding me?
Cooking was for girls.


01:02:00.612 --> 01:02:03.615
After high school,
I went backpacking through Italy.


01:02:04.866 --> 01:02:07.619
I owe my entire career
to a girl named Sophia.


01:02:07.827 --> 01:02:10.163
- Sophia?
- She's my first love.


01:02:10.789 --> 01:02:14.042
An older woman. Nineteen.


01:02:14.501 --> 01:02:16.795
Her father owned a little trattoria
in Tuscany.


01:02:16.961 --> 01:02:19.839
He was a brilliant chef and he
taught me everything he knew.


01:02:20.006 --> 01:02:23.885
Sophia told him we were just friends,
so he gave me a job in his kitchen.


01:02:24.094 --> 01:02:26.221
I fell madly in love with food.


01:02:26.388 --> 01:02:28.306
Italian food.


01:02:29.224 --> 01:02:31.184
Everything Italian, actually.


01:02:31.768 --> 01:02:33.103
So, what happened to Sophia?


01:02:33.645 --> 01:02:37.232
Her father found out
what we were up to and he fired me.


01:02:37.482 --> 01:02:41.236
- That's too bad.
- Well, it opened a lot of doors.


01:02:41.486 --> 01:02:45.824
I spent the next couple of years working
in some of the best restaurants in Milan.


01:02:46.032 --> 01:02:49.244
So how come you're not running
your own kitchen by now?


01:02:52.288 --> 01:02:53.623
I don't know.


01:02:55.083 --> 01:02:57.168
I guess the right offer
hasn't come my way.


01:03:01.923 --> 01:03:05.135
So, what would you do
if you had your wish?


01:03:05.552 --> 01:03:07.345
I got my wish.


01:03:15.395 --> 01:03:17.272
I made it this morning.


01:03:17.480 --> 01:03:21.026
- I'm not a dessert person.
- You haven't tried my tiramisu.


01:03:30.410 --> 01:03:32.579
Well, maybe I am a dessert person.


01:03:43.840 --> 01:03:48.928
You know, in Italian, "tiramisu"
means "food of the gods. "


01:03:50.847 --> 01:03:52.474
No, it doesn't.


01:03:53.767 --> 01:03:55.602
Well, it should.


01:03:59.230 --> 01:04:02.984
You have a little...
Some cream, right there.


01:04:13.453 --> 01:04:15.121
I should go.


01:04:26.841 --> 01:04:28.802
You're leaning on my scarf.


01:04:30.345 --> 01:04:32.180
Oh, right. Yeah.


01:04:32.681 --> 01:04:33.848
Sorry.


01:04:50.156 --> 01:04:51.866
Good night.


01:04:56.705 --> 01:04:59.416
<i>He's so unpredictable.</i>


01:04:59.666 --> 01:05:01.835
- In what way?
- In every way.


01:05:02.127 --> 01:05:04.754
He never does the right thing
at the right time. He's...


01:05:04.963 --> 01:05:08.049
Kate. Life is unpredictable.


01:05:08.842 --> 01:05:10.510
Not in my kitchen.


01:05:11.094 --> 01:05:13.263
I'm sure you'll be able
to prevent the worst.


01:05:15.390 --> 01:05:16.433
The worst?


01:05:17.058 --> 01:05:19.811
That he'll tolerate you
for any length of time.


01:05:20.020 --> 01:05:24.357
What is this? Some new kind of therapy?
Insult the client?


01:05:24.524 --> 01:05:26.401
Only the finest therapists use it.


01:05:31.573 --> 01:05:34.868
So I'll see you after school, okay?
Have a good day.


01:05:35.577 --> 01:05:36.870
Hello, Kate.


01:05:37.078 --> 01:05:39.414
- We're on time.
- Do you have a minute?


01:05:40.290 --> 01:05:41.791
Sure.


01:05:44.794 --> 01:05:46.880
<i>I've been speaking to Zoe's teacher.</i>


01:05:47.088 --> 01:05:49.549
She's been sleeping in class a lot.


01:05:49.758 --> 01:05:52.427
And do you know
what her explanation for this is?


01:05:52.635 --> 01:05:55.847
- No.
- She says it's her late work hours.


01:05:56.014 --> 01:05:59.142
She tells her classmates she's working
as a kitchen assistant...


01:05:59.392 --> 01:06:02.020
...in your restaurant
to earn her room and board.


01:06:03.104 --> 01:06:05.315
- I see.
- Lf I actually believed...


01:06:05.482 --> 01:06:08.026
...that Zoe was working late hours
at a restaurant...


01:06:08.193 --> 01:06:10.904
...I'd need to contact
Child Protective Services.


01:06:11.112 --> 01:06:12.947
- That won't be necessary.
- I know that.


01:06:13.323 --> 01:06:17.827
It's better for everyone when children
are well cared for by their relatives.


01:06:18.036 --> 01:06:22.207
I'd hate to see Zoe end up in foster
care after all she's been through.


01:06:22.457 --> 01:06:24.834
But I'm confident
that you will address this...


01:06:25.043 --> 01:06:27.170
...and there will be no need
to go that far.


01:06:27.420 --> 01:06:31.424
I'll be checking in on Zoe,
and we'll talk again soon.


01:06:37.430 --> 01:06:39.641
And then
Mr. Daniels' cell phone rings...


01:06:39.849 --> 01:06:44.437
...and he answers it and talks through
the whole class. It was so funny.


01:06:49.734 --> 01:06:52.487
Zoe, we need to talk about something.


01:06:55.198 --> 01:06:57.951
You can't come to work
with me anymore.


01:06:58.159 --> 01:06:59.703
Why not?


01:07:00.829 --> 01:07:03.873
Because I'm afraid they're gonna
take you away from me.


01:07:04.958 --> 01:07:07.168
- But I like going to the restaurant.
- I know.


01:07:07.377 --> 01:07:12.257
I know you do, but it's just not right for
a little girl to be up so late, you know.


01:07:12.757 --> 01:07:16.052
- You don't want me there.
- No, that's not true.


01:07:16.261 --> 01:07:19.180
No, you just need
to get a good night's rest.


01:07:19.848 --> 01:07:21.558
You hear me?


01:07:22.767 --> 01:07:24.769
You don't want to end up
being taken away.


01:07:25.020 --> 01:07:28.356
Who cares?
You didn't want me anyway.


01:07:30.900 --> 01:07:32.193
Zoe.


01:07:34.779 --> 01:07:36.072
Zoe!


01:07:37.449 --> 01:07:38.491
Zoe!


01:07:40.076 --> 01:07:41.077
Zoe!


01:07:50.754 --> 01:07:53.131
Zoe, stop it! Stop it!


01:07:53.340 --> 01:07:59.262
Let me go! Let me go!
I want my mom, not you!


01:08:09.481 --> 01:08:11.024
Zoe?


01:08:13.818 --> 01:08:16.529
- Can I come in?
- No.


01:08:17.822 --> 01:08:20.325
Zoe, please. I'm sorry.


01:08:20.575 --> 01:08:22.619
Go away.


01:08:54.651 --> 01:08:58.321
- Hi, guys. Is your dad there?
- Yeah. Dad!


01:08:58.488 --> 01:09:00.907
- Hey. Hi.
- Hi, Sean.


01:09:01.157 --> 01:09:03.827
- How are you?
- Good. Can I ask you a favor?


01:09:03.994 --> 01:09:05.829
- Of course.
- I know it's last minute...


01:09:06.037 --> 01:09:08.915
...but I have to go to work soon
and Zoe and I had a fight.


01:09:09.124 --> 01:09:10.875
You want me to keep an eye on her?


01:09:11.126 --> 01:09:15.505
- Lf you could just check on her.
- No problem. Take it inside, guys.


01:09:15.714 --> 01:09:18.508
- You got a key?
- Sure, I got it right here.


01:09:19.884 --> 01:09:21.845
- Thanks, Sean.
- Hey, how are you doing?


01:09:23.013 --> 01:09:26.057
- All this is pretty new to me.
- I know what might help.


01:09:26.558 --> 01:09:28.935
Call this number. Anna.
She's a godsend with kids.


01:09:29.185 --> 01:09:31.062
Saved me right after my divorce.


01:09:31.229 --> 01:09:34.274
I'm sure she'll be able to watch Zoe
for you whenever you need.


01:09:34.899 --> 01:09:37.402
- Thank you.
- No problem.


01:09:38.862 --> 01:09:41.656
If you're gonna play for Ireland, you're
gonna have to get stuck in better.


01:09:42.240 --> 01:09:45.368
"Ms. Armstrong introduces bits
of truffle in an endive salad...


01:09:45.577 --> 01:09:49.914
...that accompanied a lightly steamed
and wondrously silken halibut fillet.


01:09:50.123 --> 01:09:53.626
It was highlighted by the gorgeous aria
of her saffron-infused emulsion. "


01:09:53.793 --> 01:09:56.296
<i>This guy can't decide if you're a cook
or a composer:</i>


01:09:56.463 --> 01:09:59.716
"The artistry of her signature quail
with truffles made it clear...


01:09:59.883 --> 01:10:03.595
...that she brought in a great sous-chef
to complement her distinctive style. "


01:10:03.803 --> 01:10:05.180
It says that?


01:10:05.388 --> 01:10:07.766
Just making sure
you're paying attention.


01:10:09.476 --> 01:10:11.311
You look like you need a drink.


01:10:11.728 --> 01:10:13.480
I never drink at work.


01:10:27.827 --> 01:10:29.454
Are you serious?


01:10:31.122 --> 01:10:32.707
Like that?


01:10:33.124 --> 01:10:35.168
<i>Tell me what else you never do.</i>


01:10:35.960 --> 01:10:37.003
<i>What do you mean?</i>


01:10:37.253 --> 01:10:41.341
Well, you never eat dessert.
You never drink at work.


01:10:42.384 --> 01:10:46.471
I'm kind of hoping you'll tell me you
never go out with guys who sing opera.


01:10:47.013 --> 01:10:49.683
I never go out with guys
who sing opera.


01:10:53.186 --> 01:10:54.771
Yes.


01:11:05.782 --> 01:11:08.243
- I got it.
- I got it.


01:11:15.267 --> 01:11:17.561
So I've got one for you.


01:11:17.769 --> 01:11:21.982
What are the three secrets
of French cuisine?


01:11:22.190 --> 01:11:24.901
Oh, come on. Everybody knows that.


01:11:25.110 --> 01:11:28.447
Oh, yeah?
So, what are they, smarty-pants?


01:11:28.989 --> 01:11:32.451
Butter, butter and butter.


01:11:33.035 --> 01:11:34.912
You're good.


01:11:35.662 --> 01:11:39.625
You know, you didn't have to do this.
It's not like I'm drunk or anything.


01:11:40.792 --> 01:11:42.711
Sean. Hi.


01:11:44.671 --> 01:11:46.965
Nick, this is Sean, he lives downstairs.


01:11:47.299 --> 01:11:49.760
This is Nick. We cook together.


01:11:50.010 --> 01:11:52.721
- How are you?
- You obviously don't live in the building.


01:11:53.639 --> 01:11:57.976
- How was Zoe?
- Sound asleep. She's a great kid.


01:11:58.310 --> 01:12:00.646
- Have a good night.
- Thanks, Sean.


01:12:01.647 --> 01:12:03.815
Yeah, he's so sweet.


01:12:04.358 --> 01:12:07.194
He was just keeping an eye on Zoe.


01:12:07.444 --> 01:12:11.156
He's just a sweet, nice guy.
I couldn't wish for a better neighbor.


01:12:11.365 --> 01:12:14.159
Yeah, he's always just so...


01:12:16.578 --> 01:12:18.872
in a totally neigh...


01:12:24.586 --> 01:12:26.463
Take an aspirin.


01:12:28.257 --> 01:12:29.675
Yeah.


01:13:05.377 --> 01:13:06.795
<i>Come on!</i>


01:14:31.880 --> 01:14:34.132
It's time to get up, sweetheart.


01:14:37.719 --> 01:14:40.264
I don't wanna go to school today.


01:14:41.723 --> 01:14:43.517
Guess what.


01:14:45.018 --> 01:14:47.354
I don't wanna go to work today.


01:14:48.647 --> 01:14:50.232
Really?


01:14:52.276 --> 01:14:54.778
Today it's just gonna be you and me.


01:15:08.292 --> 01:15:10.377
"To all the gang at 22 Bleecker...


01:15:10.544 --> 01:15:13.797
...let me introduce you
to my little hors d'oeuvre. "


01:15:14.047 --> 01:15:16.550
- Let's see the photo.
- Emma Jillian. Here we go.


01:15:16.758 --> 01:15:20.220
- "Seven pounds, three ounces. "
- She's adorable.


01:15:20.429 --> 01:15:24.683
"She can't wait to meet you all.
Love and kisses, Leah. "


01:15:25.684 --> 01:15:27.477
Kate's late.


01:15:28.395 --> 01:15:32.816
She asked for some time off.
Something personal came up.


01:15:33.817 --> 01:15:36.737
One, two, three, four, five, six!
Yes, Park Place!


01:15:36.945 --> 01:15:41.491
- And with a hotel, 1500 bucks.
- I don't have enough.


01:15:41.909 --> 01:15:43.619
Mortgage, baby. Mortgage.


01:15:43.827 --> 01:15:46.455
Come on. I love this game.


01:15:48.457 --> 01:15:49.499
Come on.


01:15:51.293 --> 01:15:54.755
All right. Great. Thank you.
All right, so, what do I need?


01:15:54.963 --> 01:15:58.842
I need a nine. Give me a nine
and it's Free Parking.


01:15:59.051 --> 01:16:01.345
Oh, boy. Here we go.


01:16:04.514 --> 01:16:06.850
- Yes!
- No!


01:16:07.059 --> 01:16:08.810
This isn't fair. No!


01:16:09.269 --> 01:16:14.483
I'm rich. I'm rich. I'm rich!


01:16:17.277 --> 01:16:19.446
You know what this means,
don't you?


01:16:19.655 --> 01:16:21.198
- No, what does it mean?
- War!


01:16:46.515 --> 01:16:49.643
Come on and fight!
You're afraid of a little pillow?


01:17:01.905 --> 01:17:04.575
How's that rib eye doing, you guys?
I need two sea bass.


01:17:04.825 --> 01:17:08.537
All right, pancetta, goat cheese, oysters,
steak tartare, grilled rib eye.


01:17:08.745 --> 01:17:11.540
- How much longer on that rib eye, Mario?
- Rib eye coming.


01:17:11.748 --> 01:17:13.542
Come on, let's pick it up.


01:17:16.378 --> 01:17:18.922
I needed that soufflé five minutes ago.
Let's go.


01:17:28.348 --> 01:17:33.478
<i>We did 110 covers tonight.
Everything was excellent.</i>


01:17:33.854 --> 01:17:35.606
You've really
mastered the menu, Nick.


01:17:35.856 --> 01:17:41.069
You put your signature on the dishes,
and all the regulars have noticed.


01:17:44.114 --> 01:17:47.784
How would you like
to stay on permanently?


01:17:51.663 --> 01:17:53.373
I think I'd like that.


01:17:54.166 --> 01:17:56.126
If it's okay with Kate.


01:18:23.070 --> 01:18:26.198
<i>- Who is it?
- Do you have any idea what time it is?</i>


01:18:26.949 --> 01:18:29.743
<i>- What?
- It's very, very late.</i>


01:18:38.961 --> 01:18:42.881
The kitchen was a very different place
without you tonight.


01:18:43.757 --> 01:18:45.884
I'm sure you did just fine without me.


01:18:50.847 --> 01:18:53.767
- It was hell.
- That's better.


01:19:03.735 --> 01:19:05.237
Cognac...


01:19:06.488 --> 01:19:07.906
...white wine...


01:19:09.283 --> 01:19:10.617
...celery...


01:19:12.536 --> 01:19:14.830
...leek, shallots...


01:19:16.290 --> 01:19:17.916
...and garlic.


01:19:49.239 --> 01:19:50.949
I'm getting truffle.


01:20:02.044 --> 01:20:05.172
- I haven't... I think I...
- Don't think.


01:20:40.916 --> 01:20:43.293
Pancake time.


01:20:47.506 --> 01:20:49.800
Pancake time.


01:20:50.634 --> 01:20:52.594
Where's my sous-chef?


01:20:53.595 --> 01:20:56.598
- Pancakes?
- You want to help me?


01:20:57.474 --> 01:20:59.434
Okay, flip it.


01:21:00.143 --> 01:21:05.107
Nice. You could start
your own restaurant. Call it Zoe's.


01:21:05.315 --> 01:21:07.067
I'll call it Nick and Zoe's.


01:21:07.276 --> 01:21:09.695
Excuse me?
I did squeeze the orange juice.


01:21:09.987 --> 01:21:13.907
Okay. Nick and Kate and Zoe's.


01:21:14.157 --> 01:21:15.617
I like the ring of that.


01:21:18.662 --> 01:21:19.871
Not in front of Zoe.


01:21:20.664 --> 01:21:23.250
Zoe, I'm now going to kiss your aunt.


01:21:24.293 --> 01:21:26.837
This is so embarrassing.


01:21:32.926 --> 01:21:35.512
So how are we gonna
work together now?


01:21:35.679 --> 01:21:37.180
We'll do what we always did.


01:21:37.347 --> 01:21:38.724
You tell me what to do...


01:21:38.890 --> 01:21:41.935
...and I'll go behind your back
and do whatever I want.


01:22:07.886 --> 01:22:11.515
I wanna show you something.
Quick! Let's go.


01:22:14.768 --> 01:22:17.896
Excuse me.
Do you have any kaffir lime leaves?


01:22:18.105 --> 01:22:20.941
- Over there. You touch, you buy.
- I know, I know.


01:22:22.025 --> 01:22:25.112
- What do you need those for?
- You'll see.


01:22:26.071 --> 01:22:27.656
Here they are.


01:22:27.948 --> 01:22:30.284
- One for you.
- Smells good.


01:22:30.534 --> 01:22:33.245
Like it? One for you.


01:22:34.163 --> 01:22:35.831
How do I know this smell?


01:22:37.249 --> 01:22:39.293
Is this your saffron sauce?


01:22:40.294 --> 01:22:42.171
Apparently we have
no secrets anymore.


01:22:42.421 --> 01:22:43.922
You touch.


01:22:44.131 --> 01:22:45.924
I know. I buy.


01:22:46.258 --> 01:22:48.761
- You buy.
- Two dollar.


01:23:35.474 --> 01:23:37.976
Today for our entrée special,
we are offering...


01:23:38.185 --> 01:23:41.146
...a Hudson Valley free-range duck...


01:23:41.355 --> 01:23:44.650
...over a butternut-squash purée...


01:23:44.858 --> 01:23:49.405
...and that is served with
patty pan squash and blood orange...


01:23:49.655 --> 01:23:52.700
...and finished with
a mushroom sauce made up...


01:23:52.908 --> 01:23:55.661
...of a variety of wild mushrooms...
- From the...


01:23:55.869 --> 01:23:57.871
from the cognac region of France.


01:23:58.080 --> 01:24:00.165
- What do you think?
- What's that?


01:24:00.374 --> 01:24:05.295
Nick came up with a great idea
of sending mini desserts home in a box.


01:24:05.921 --> 01:24:07.715
It's so obvious.


01:24:09.174 --> 01:24:10.801
So obvious.


01:24:11.009 --> 01:24:14.054
And, Nick, I love those wines
you recommended for the new menu.


01:24:14.221 --> 01:24:17.099
Well, you're gonna have to
discuss that with Kate.


01:24:18.934 --> 01:24:20.811
John, tell us
about the asparagus dish.


01:24:22.062 --> 01:24:26.275
We're also serving as a special
a side...


01:24:26.483 --> 01:24:30.112
Rather, an appetizer
with asparagus and cippolini onions...


01:24:30.320 --> 01:24:33.282
...and it has a side
of sliced watermelon radishes.


01:24:33.782 --> 01:24:37.202
Table five's coming up in two seconds,
chef.


01:24:47.588 --> 01:24:50.799
Nick, the couple at table eight
wants to say hello.


01:24:50.966 --> 01:24:54.511
- They're drooling over the sea bass.
- Kate's responsible for all the food.


01:24:54.762 --> 01:24:57.097
- She hates leaving the kitchen.
- Interesting.


01:24:57.306 --> 01:24:59.975
- What else can you tell us about her?
- You know what?


01:25:00.225 --> 01:25:03.145
I'm not gonna get into this.
I don't care who goes out there.


01:25:03.353 --> 01:25:08.984
But if it is you, do me a favor and try
not to stab anyone who complains.


01:25:09.034 --> 01:25:10.911
Don't look at me.


01:25:11.120 --> 01:25:14.123
You. Me. In there. Now.


01:25:23.465 --> 01:25:25.426
- So, what's the story?
- What do you mean?


01:25:25.593 --> 01:25:27.761
I turn my back
for a couple of days and it's:


01:25:27.928 --> 01:25:30.639
"Nick, the wine. Nick, the customers.
Nick, the boxes... "


01:25:30.806 --> 01:25:32.349
She offered me your job.


01:25:33.601 --> 01:25:35.060
What?


01:25:36.687 --> 01:25:38.564
Why didn't you tell me?


01:25:39.356 --> 01:25:41.692
- I can't believe this.
- I was going to tell you.


01:25:41.859 --> 01:25:43.360
I knew I couldn't trust you.


01:25:43.527 --> 01:25:47.114
- The moment I met you, I knew.
- The truth is that you can't trust anyone.


01:25:47.281 --> 01:25:49.867
- You've never trusted anyone in your life.
- Guess what.


01:25:50.075 --> 01:25:51.869
Why should I when this happens?


01:25:52.244 --> 01:25:55.372
Why didn't you have the guts
just to run your own kitchen, Nick?


01:25:55.539 --> 01:25:57.791
Instead of coming in here
and taking over mine?


01:25:58.000 --> 01:26:00.711
- Is that what you think?
- That's exactly what I think.


01:26:06.842 --> 01:26:08.969
You know, Kate...


01:26:11.514 --> 01:26:15.309
...it's okay to let people in sometimes.
Maybe one of these days...


01:26:15.476 --> 01:26:17.853
...you'll figure that out.
- You don't understand.


01:26:18.062 --> 01:26:20.147
This place is my life.


01:26:20.689 --> 01:26:23.651
- This is who I am.
- No, it's not who you are.


01:26:24.860 --> 01:26:26.862
It's only one little part.


01:26:37.456 --> 01:26:39.250
Anna, it's me.


01:26:39.583 --> 01:26:40.960
Hi.


01:26:45.464 --> 01:26:46.882
How did everything go?


01:26:47.091 --> 01:26:50.219
I think we did well.
We played Monopoly.


01:26:50.427 --> 01:26:53.264
- Who won?
- She did.


01:26:54.890 --> 01:26:56.183
Thanks a lot, Anna.


01:26:56.392 --> 01:26:58.769
- See you tomorrow.
- Good night.


01:27:14.410 --> 01:27:19.248
<i>Mailbox one.
You have one new message.</i>


01:27:19.415 --> 01:27:23.836
<i>Monday, 11:54 p. m.</i>


01:27:24.086 --> 01:27:28.924
<i>Oh, and for the record,
I did turn her down.</i>


01:27:32.136 --> 01:27:34.763
<i>End of messages.</i>


01:27:38.225 --> 01:27:42.980
<i>Oh, and for the record,
I did turn her down.</i>


01:27:48.485 --> 01:27:49.528
Kate.


01:27:51.614 --> 01:27:53.115
Still awake?


01:27:53.741 --> 01:27:55.284
Where's Nick?


01:27:57.244 --> 01:27:58.829
He went home after work.


01:28:01.165 --> 01:28:03.459
Get some sleep, it's late.


01:28:06.128 --> 01:28:08.339
- Kate?
- Yeah?


01:28:11.133 --> 01:28:13.511
You can sleep with Louie if you want.


01:28:17.681 --> 01:28:20.476
Oh, honey, that's sweet of you.


01:28:20.893 --> 01:28:22.770
He needs you, I'm fine.


01:28:23.854 --> 01:28:25.356
Night-night.


01:28:30.903 --> 01:28:32.196
Night.


01:28:38.244 --> 01:28:41.539
You had no right driving him out of here.
This is my restaurant.


01:28:41.705 --> 01:28:45.334
- You've made that abundantly clear.
- You better find me a replacement fast.


01:28:45.543 --> 01:28:47.545
You didn't need my help
with the last one.


01:28:47.753 --> 01:28:50.631
- Kate.
- Okay. I'll find someone.


01:28:53.717 --> 01:28:57.221
Like a certificate or something?
I don't have that little piece of paper.


01:28:57.429 --> 01:29:00.224
But there's guys driving
on the street without a license.


01:29:00.432 --> 01:29:02.101
They can't drive, so, you know.


01:29:02.351 --> 01:29:04.270
Well, my specialty is in the beef area.


01:29:04.478 --> 01:29:08.691
I deal with meats all the time.
Sausage, beef, slaughtering pork.


01:29:08.899 --> 01:29:10.943
I'm famous
for my Vietnamese pork chops...


01:29:11.151 --> 01:29:13.779
...with saffron mashed potatoes
and key-lime asparagus.


01:29:13.946 --> 01:29:17.741
I get along great with people.
Really, I'm actually a big people person.


01:29:17.950 --> 01:29:19.743
Oh, I'm a people person.


01:29:19.910 --> 01:29:22.413
I'm a team player so long
as everybody follows my lead.


01:29:22.580 --> 01:29:26.709
There was a misunderstanding
between me and the head chef...


01:29:26.917 --> 01:29:29.378
...and the manager and the owners.


01:29:29.587 --> 01:29:32.298
Fired is like, you know, it's,
"You're fired!" You know.


01:29:32.464 --> 01:29:36.886
But, no, I think we parted
on amicable terms.


01:29:43.601 --> 01:29:46.687
Why doesn't Nick
come to see us anymore?


01:29:51.275 --> 01:29:53.986
We had kind of a fight.


01:29:54.486 --> 01:29:58.199
- What about?
- Just silly grown-up stuff.


01:30:02.995 --> 01:30:04.997
How come you don't wanna tell me?


01:30:07.458 --> 01:30:11.003
- It's not that I don't wanna tell you.
- Is he ever gonna come back?


01:30:11.837 --> 01:30:14.215
No, he isn't, sweetheart.


01:30:26.852 --> 01:30:28.646
Zoe.


01:30:59.009 --> 01:31:00.970
Zoe, you awake?


01:31:01.971 --> 01:31:03.556
I'm done.


01:31:04.682 --> 01:31:06.600
Are you having breakfast?


01:31:11.689 --> 01:31:12.982
Zoe?


01:31:16.569 --> 01:31:19.196
Nick, it's me.
Is Zoe with you?


01:31:20.281 --> 01:31:22.241
I got up this morning,
and she was gone.


01:31:22.783 --> 01:31:25.160
I'm here right now.
They haven't seen her.


01:31:26.245 --> 01:31:30.666
I don't know. I told her about us
last night and she was upset, but...


01:31:30.833 --> 01:31:32.793
Oh, my God.


01:31:33.002 --> 01:31:34.170
What did the police say?


01:31:34.336 --> 01:31:37.882
They checked the bus station and the
train station. She could be anywhere.


01:31:38.048 --> 01:31:41.719
Well, she's a kid. She would probably
choose someplace she knew, right?


01:31:41.886 --> 01:31:44.555
She went to school and the restaurant,
that's it.


01:31:51.562 --> 01:31:54.899
Kate, it's gonna be fine.
She's gonna be all right.


01:31:55.065 --> 01:31:58.569
You know what, maybe we should check
if she's gone back home.


01:31:59.486 --> 01:32:01.197
Zoe?


01:32:02.448 --> 01:32:04.742
Maybe she left a note somewhere.


01:32:05.326 --> 01:32:07.161
She's not here.


01:32:17.588 --> 01:32:21.008
Did she take her backpack?
If she didn't pack anything...


01:32:21.175 --> 01:32:23.469
- She didn't take Louie.
- What?


01:32:24.470 --> 01:32:27.890
She wouldn't run away
without Louie, right?


01:32:28.474 --> 01:32:31.602
I let her down, Nick. I feel like
I made a mess of everything.


01:32:31.810 --> 01:32:34.647
- We're gonna find her. I promise.
- She needs her mother.


01:32:34.813 --> 01:32:36.690
- She just needs her mother.
- Kate.


01:32:38.651 --> 01:32:40.694
I think I know where she might be.


01:32:45.908 --> 01:32:49.328
- There she is right there.
- Oh, thank God.


01:32:52.414 --> 01:32:54.667
Zoe, are you all right?


01:32:56.043 --> 01:32:58.254
Zoe, please, don't ever do that again.


01:32:58.420 --> 01:33:00.923
I was so afraid
something happened to you.


01:33:02.383 --> 01:33:04.885
Sweetheart, what is it?


01:33:06.762 --> 01:33:09.181
I'm afraid I'm gonna forget her.


01:33:13.018 --> 01:33:14.937
We'll never forget her.


01:33:15.729 --> 01:33:17.189
I promise.


01:33:22.194 --> 01:33:23.737
Never.


01:33:35.875 --> 01:33:38.919
And we can come here
whenever you want, okay?


01:34:07.364 --> 01:34:09.074
You're coming in, aren't you, Nick?


01:34:09.867 --> 01:34:11.327
Not today, sweetie.


01:34:12.036 --> 01:34:14.830
- Guys still mad at each other?
- No.


01:34:15.372 --> 01:34:16.832
Come on.


01:34:22.630 --> 01:34:24.173
See you upstairs.


01:34:27.551 --> 01:34:29.011
- You know...
- You know...


01:34:31.013 --> 01:34:32.640
I just wanna say I'm sorry, Nick.


01:34:32.806 --> 01:34:34.892
Don't apologize.
I actually wanna thank you.


01:34:35.059 --> 01:34:37.186
I thought a lot about what you said...


01:34:37.353 --> 01:34:41.273
...about me not having the guts to go
after what I want, and you were right.


01:34:42.274 --> 01:34:43.776
That's why...


01:34:45.027 --> 01:34:46.445
...I took a job.


01:34:47.196 --> 01:34:48.822
In San Francisco.


01:34:49.198 --> 01:34:53.536
The executive chef
at a new restaurant.


01:34:57.790 --> 01:34:59.792
- Well, that's great.
- Yeah.


01:35:01.210 --> 01:35:03.879
Well, I couldn't have done it
without you.


01:35:16.600 --> 01:35:18.519
Executive chef.


01:35:36.328 --> 01:35:38.747
Guy at table seven said
if he wanted it cremated...


01:35:38.914 --> 01:35:40.833
...he wouldn't have asked for it rare.


01:35:41.834 --> 01:35:44.253
- That is rare.
- Apparently not rare enough.


01:35:44.420 --> 01:35:46.755
Any rarer, it'd walk out of here
and hail a cab.


01:35:46.964 --> 01:35:50.092
Look, these are ad-agency people.
They spend a lot of money here.


01:35:50.259 --> 01:35:53.345
No tantrums tonight.
Just fire another one.


01:35:55.848 --> 01:35:59.435
- Fire one rare steak on the fly.
- Rare steak on the fly.


01:35:59.602 --> 01:36:01.729
Where is the lamb for six?


01:36:01.896 --> 01:36:03.439
- How are the quail?
- Great, chef.


01:36:03.606 --> 01:36:06.567
Pick up! Terrine, carpaccio.


01:36:09.653 --> 01:36:12.156
From the asshole on seven again.
He wants to know...


01:36:12.364 --> 01:36:15.618
...whether you've ever seen
a rare steak before.


01:36:26.879 --> 01:36:29.173
- Rare enough for you?
- Are you out of your mind?


01:36:29.340 --> 01:36:31.509
- Yeah. That's why I'm in therapy.
- I'm so sorry.


01:36:31.675 --> 01:36:34.845
I'll get you a new tablecloth.


01:36:35.054 --> 01:36:37.515
No, please, let me take care of that.


01:36:38.974 --> 01:36:40.893
Not bad.


01:36:41.435 --> 01:36:43.646
That felt so good.


01:36:47.816 --> 01:36:49.568
I just want a steak.


01:36:53.739 --> 01:36:56.742
<i>I wish there was a cookbook for life,
you know?</i>


01:36:56.951 --> 01:36:59.453
<i>With the recipes
telling us exactly what to do.</i>


01:37:01.288 --> 01:37:05.793
I know. I know. You're gonna say,
"How else can we learn, Kate?"


01:37:05.960 --> 01:37:09.046
No. Actually, I wasn't gonna say that.


01:37:09.797 --> 01:37:12.424
- You wanna guess again?
- Oh, no, go ahead.


01:37:13.259 --> 01:37:17.137
What I was gonna say was
you know better than anyone.


01:37:17.888 --> 01:37:21.183
It's the recipes you create yourself
that are the best.


01:37:50.546 --> 01:37:52.506
Hold on just a second.


01:37:57.720 --> 01:38:00.598
I think you should know
there's something else I never do.


01:38:01.307 --> 01:38:02.558
What's that?


01:38:02.766 --> 01:38:05.728
I never invite myself
into a man's apartment, blindfold him...


01:38:05.936 --> 01:38:11.525
...and feed him saffron sauce while
begging him not to go to San Francisco.


01:38:12.234 --> 01:38:14.320
- You never do that?
- Never.


01:38:14.528 --> 01:38:16.155
That's too bad.


01:38:54.818 --> 01:38:58.113
- You're gonna sear that first, right?
- Yeah, chef.


01:39:02.368 --> 01:39:05.287
Don't forget to reduce
this sauce a little, okay?


01:39:05.454 --> 01:39:07.164
- You're crossing the line.
- No.


01:39:07.331 --> 01:39:10.501
Yes, you are.
Look, your spoon's in my territory.


01:39:11.544 --> 01:39:15.297
Look, I can't help if your reduction's
a little thin. I have to say something.


01:39:15.464 --> 01:39:18.092
I wouldn't talk.
Your sabayon's got lumps.


01:39:19.552 --> 01:39:21.095
You're out of your mind.


01:39:24.431 --> 01:39:27.101
- It's perfect.
- I'll be the judge of that.


01:39:41.156 --> 01:39:43.242
You're right, it is perfect.


01:39:46.036 --> 01:39:47.705
Pancakes.


01:39:49.456 --> 01:39:51.959
- Thank you.
- Voilà.


01:39:54.170 --> 01:39:56.380
Zoe, that's enough.


01:40:00.259 --> 01:40:01.886
- Hi.
- Hi.


01:40:13.439 --> 01:40:15.524
Hey, Zoe. Thank you.


01:40:15.733 --> 01:40:18.903
Wait. Let her tell us what.
What have we got?


01:40:18.904 --> 01:40:29.904
<i>SiNCRONiZACiON POR
~ N3krA ~
SEPTiCEMiA TEAM
.::Piratas Con Los Patines::.</i>

